// Akoma Ntoso 1.0: the graph model and sample data
//
// Generated by ../../cypher.py from model.json and sample.json. Edit those and regenerate, rather than this file.
//
// A fictional amending act, the Consumer Protection (Amendment) Act, 2024 of a fictional jurisdiction (country code
// zz, which ISO 3166 leaves to users), with its FRBR identification, publication, lifecycle, references,
// classification and the structure of its preamble and body down to articles, paragraphs and the people, terms and
// dates their text refers to. An article of the Act substitutes an article of the principal act, the Consumer
// Protection Act, 2012: the Act's analysis records it as an active textual modification with its source, destination
// and period, and the principal act, kept as a document of its own, records the same change as a passive
// modification.
//
// Run it against an empty database of Neo4j 5 or later, Enterprise Edition, for its node key and property existence
// constraints, e.g. with cypher-shell -f model.cypher. It merges every node and relationship, so it can be run again.

// The model: its constraints

